\ Plain (non-protocol) generic dispatch in interpreter-free AOT. A method is
\ registered on the built-in `fixnum`; the call site routes through the
\ generic dispatch helper, which finds the replayed method and runs it. If the
\ method did not replay, the generic's default body divides by zero and the
\ binary exits non-zero. A clean exit proves the method dispatched. No virtual
\ types or printing, so the binary links no interpreter.

bump: generic ( x -- n ) [ 0 / ] ;
bump: method{ fixnum } [ 1 + ] ;

5 bump drop
